    dinDefTitle: "Cos'è la regolazione DIN degli attacchi da sci?",
    dinDefP1: "Il valore DIN (denominato secondo gli standard del Deutsches Institut für Normung) è un indice numerico calibrato che stabilisce la coppia di sgancio dell'attacco da sci alpino. Determina l'entità della forza torcente o flettente richiesta per liberare lo scarpone durante una caduta.",
    dinDefP2: "La tabella ufficiale ISO 11088 definisce valori indicativi compresi tra 0,75 e 12,00. Gli sciatori principianti necessitano in genere di valori tra 2 e 5, mentre gli atleti e freerider esperti utilizzano attacchi che superano questo intervallo fino a 14, 16 o più. Un DIN troppo basso comporta lo sgancio accidentale dello sci durante la curva; un DIN eccessivamente alto impedisce l'apertura in caduta, aumentando notevolmente il rischio di lesioni a legamenti e ossa.",
    isoMattersTitle: "Perché la norma ISO 11088:2023 è fondamentale",
    isoMattersP1: "La norma internazionale ISO 11088 definisce le procedure di montaggio, regolazione e ispezione del sistema integrato sci-attacco-scarpone. Essa stabilisce il legame matematico rigoroso tra i parametri fisici dello sciatore — peso, altezza, età e lunghezza scafo — e la corretta forza di sgancio.",
    isoMattersP2: "DIN Calculator Pro applica integralmente la revisione ISO 11088:2023 (Edizione 7, che supera e sostituisce l'edizione 2018 ritirata). Ogni valore calcolato deriva direttamente dalle matrici ufficiali, con arbitri altezza-peso e correzioni per età e stile di sciata.",
    fourStepTitle: "Il metodo di calcolo ISO 11088 in 4 passaggi",
    fourStep1Title: "Determinare il codice sciatore iniziale.",
    fourStep1Desc: "Peso corporeo e altezza individuano una riga iniziale (dalla lettera A alla M). Qualora altezza e peso indichino righe differenti, la norma ISO impone di scegliere la riga più in alto nella tabella (lettera inferiore) per garantire la massima cautela.",
    fourStep2Title: "Applicare il fattore stile di sciata.",
    fourStep2Desc: "Il Tipo I rimane sulla riga base. Il Tipo II scende di 1 riga (+1 lettera, valore DIN più alto). Il Tipo III scende di 2 righe (+2 lettere). Il Tipo III+ scende di 3 righe. Il Tipo −I sale di 1 riga (-1 lettera per sciatori sopra i 17 kg). Agli sciatori fino a 13 kg non si applica alcuna modifica.",
    fourStep3Title: "Applicare la correzione per età.",
    fourStep3Desc: "Gli sciatori sotto i 10 anni o a partire dai 50 anni salgono di 1 riga nella matrice (-1 lettera / DIN inferiore) per proteggere le articolazioni e preservare la sicurezza ossea.",
    fourStep4Title: "Incrociare con la lunghezza scafo (BSL in mm).",
    fourStep4Desc: "Il codice sciatore definitivo individua la riga nella tabella ISO 11088; la lunghezza scafo in millimetri dello scarpone individua la colonna. La cella di incrocio restituisce la taratura DIN indicativa.",
    bslTitle: "Che cos'è la lunghezza scafo dello scarpone (BSL)?",
    bslP1: "La lunghezza scafo (Boot Sole Length o BSL) è la misura fisica esterna totale della suola dello scarpone in millimetri, rilevata dal puntale alla talloniera. È impressa in rilievo lateralmente o sotto il tallone di ogni scarpone da sci alpino. La BSL è completamente diversa dalla taglia Mondopoint (misura del piede in cm): scarponi con la stessa misura Mondo 27.5 possono avere lunghezze scafo comprese tra 298 mm e 320 mm a seconda del produttore.",
    bslP2: "La BSL incide in modo determinante sulla taratura poiché uno scarpone più lungo esercita una leva maggiore sull'attacco. Usa sempre il valore millimetrico effettivo impresso sullo scarpone — non stimarlo mai dalla misura delle scarpe da ginnastica.",
    bslLinkText: "Guida a BSL e taglie Mondopoint →",
    skierTypeTitle: "Come scegliere il tipo di sciatore",
    skierTypeP1: "La corretta classificazione dello sciatore è cruciale: un'auto-valutazione errata è il motivo più comune di regolazione errata. La norma ISO 11088 individua quattro categorie:",
    skierTypeMinusI: "Sciatori principianti estremamente prudenti e bambini che sciano solo su pendii dolci a velocità minima.",
    skierTypeI: "Sciatori prudenti che sciano a velocità moderata su piste battute facili. Priorità assoluta allo sgancio immediato per proteggere le ginocchia.",
    skierTypeII: "Sciatori di medio livello che sciano a velocità moderata o sostenuta su terreni variati. È la scelta corretta per la maggioranza degli adulti.",
    skierTypeIII: "Sciatori esperti e aggressivi che affrontano piste ripide e neve difficile ad alta velocità. Priorità alla tenuta meccanica dell'attacco.",
    skierTypeP2: "La stragrande maggioranza degli sciatori ricreativi rientra nel Tipo I o Tipo II. Sovrastimarsi come Tipo III quando non si hanno le velocità richieste genera tarature pericolosamente elevate.",
    safetyTitle: "Il calcolatore online è sicuro senza l'intervento di uno skiman?",
    safetyP1: "DIN Calculator Pro fornisce un valore di riferimento scientifico basato sulle tabelle ufficiali ISO 11088:2023. Questo valore è un punto di partenza fondamentale, ma non può sostituire il controllo pratico in laboratorio sci. La regolazione meccanica, la verifica del precarico (spinta longitudinale) e il controllo dello sgancio devono essere sempre effettuati da uno skiman certificato con banco di prova calibrato.",
    safetyP2: "Lo sgancio reale dipende da parametri fisici che nessun software può analizzare: l'usura degli inserti della suola, lo stato della piastrina antifrizione (AFD), la tensione della molla e l'invecchiamento dei meccanismi. Solo un macchinario dinamometrico da laboratorio misura la coppia effettiva.",
    safetyWorkflowTitle: "La procedura corretta raccomandata:",
    safetyWorkflowText: "Calcola il tuo valore indicativo su DIN Calculator Pro, stampa o salva la tua scheda tecnica, e consegna la tua attrezzatura a un laboratorio sci specializzato per il montaggio, la regolazione della spinta e la prova dinamometrica secondo gli standard ISO 11088 e ASTM F1063.",
    subLinksMatrixTitle: "Matrice ISO 11088",
    subLinksMatrixDesc: "Tabella DIN completa",
    subLinksBslTitle: "Guida Scafo BSL",
    subLinksBslDesc: "Trova la misura in mm",
    subLinksSkierTypesTitle: "Tipi di Sciatore",
    subLinksSkierTypesDesc: "Guida a Tipo I, II, III"
  },
  en: {
    quickAnswerBadge: 'Quick Answer & Reference Guide',
    quickAnswerH2: 'What DIN Setting Do You Need?',
    quickAnswerP: 'A ski binding DIN setting controls the force required to release your boot safely during a fall. Calculated under ISO 11088:2023, your baseline code is determined by your weight and height, adjusted for skier type (-I to III+) and age group, and finally mapped against your boot sole length (BSL in mm).',
    exampleTitle: 'Worked Calculation Example',
    profile: 'Skier Profile:',
    profileVal: '75 kg (165 lbs), 178 cm, 30 yrs, Type II, BSL 305mm',
    step1: 'Step 1 — Weight Code (67–78 kg):',
    step2: 'Step 2 — Height Code (167–178 cm):',
    step3: 'Step 3 — Baseline Determination:',
    step3Val: 'Code K (Agreement)',
    step4: 'Step 4 — Skier Type II Shift:',
    step4Val: '+1 Row Shift → Code L',
    step5: 'Step 5 — Age Modifier (30 years):',
    step5Val: '0 Modifier (Adult) → Final Code L',
    step6: 'Step 6 — BSL 305 mm Lookup:',
    note: 'Note: All calculations provide a baseline setting. Final release calibration must be verified on diagnostic test equipment by a trained ski technician.',
    tableTitle: 'Baseline DIN by Weight (BSL 305 mm, Adult)',
    tableWeight: 'Skier Weight',
    tableType1: 'Type I (Beginner)',
    tableType2: 'Type II (All-Mtn)',
    tableType3: 'Type III (Aggressive)',
    exploreMore: 'Explore all boot sole lengths and skier codes:',
    fullMatrixLink: 'Full ISO 11088 Matrix →',
    pillars: [
      { title: "Based on ISO 11088:2023", desc: "Implements the full ISO 11088:2023 matrix including height-weight conflict resolution, age modifiers, and horizontal nearest-neighbor fallback logic." },
      { title: "Zero-Data Architecture", desc: "All calculations run in browser RAM. Your weight, height, age, and boot size are never sent to a server, stored in cookies, or logged anywhere." },
      { title: "Technician Export Card", desc: "Export a clean, printable summary card with your DIN settings to share with a trained ski technician for binding mounting and calibration." }
    ],
    methodologyH2: "How the ISO 11088 math works.",
    methodologyDesc: "A transparent, step-by-step breakdown of how your DIN value is calculated.",
    methodologySteps: [
      { step: "01", title: "Baseline Force", desc: "Body weight and height determine your initial Skier Code and safe threshold." },
      { step: "02", title: "Ability Shift", desc: "Your Skier Type modifies the code: Type I uses the baseline row, Type II moves 1 row lower on the chart, Type III moves 2 rows lower." },
      { step: "03", title: "Age Modifier", desc: "Skiers under 10 or age 50+ move 1 row higher on the chart (lower DIN) for bone and joint safety." },
      { step: "04", title: "Matrix Lookup", desc: "Your final Skier Code intersects with your Boot Sole Length on the ISO 11088:2023 matrix." }
    ],
    guideH2: "Understanding Your Ski Binding DIN Setting",
    guideDesc: "Everything you need to know about ski binding release settings, ISO 11088 compliance, and how to use a DIN calculator safely.",
    dinDefTitle: "What Is a DIN Setting?",
    dinDefP1: "A DIN setting (named after Deutsches Institut für Normung, the German Institute for Standardization) is a calibrated numeric value that defines the release torque of your alpine ski binding. It determines how much twisting or bending force must be applied to your boot before the binding releases it from the ski.",
    dinDefP2: "The standard ISO 11088 lookup matrix defines release values ranging from 0.75 to 12.00. Recreational beginner skiers typically need settings between 2 and 5, while adult competition and freeride bindings scale beyond this table to 14, 16, or higher. Setting your DIN too low risks accidental pre-release during turns; setting it too high prevents release during a crash, increasing injury risk.",
    isoMattersTitle: "Why ISO 11088:2023 Matters",
    isoMattersP1: "ISO 11088 is the international standard that governs how alpine ski bindings are assembled, inspected, and adjusted. It defines the mathematical relationship between a skier's physical characteristics — weight, height, age, and boot sole length — and the appropriate release setting.",
    isoMattersP2: "DIN Calculator Pro implements ISO 11088:2023 (Edition 7, which supersedes the withdrawn 2018 edition). Every calculation is derived from standard weight-height lookup tables, modified by exact skier type row offsets and age adjustments defined in the standard.",
    fourStepTitle: "The Four-Step ISO 11088 Calculation Method",
    fourStep1Title: "Determine your initial Skier Code.",
    fourStep1Desc: "Body weight and height produce an initial Skier Code (A through M). Where height and weight suggest different codes, the ISO standard mandates selecting the row closer to the top of the chart (lower code) for conservative safety.",
    fourStep2Title: "Apply the Skier Type modifier.",
    fourStep2Desc: "Type I uses the baseline row. Type II moves one row lower on the chart (+1 code, higher DIN). Type III moves two rows lower (+2 codes). Type III+ moves three rows lower (+3 codes, manufacturer convention). Type −I moves one row higher (-1 code, for skiers over 17 kg). Skiers weighing 13 kg or less receive no ability modifier.",
    fourStep3Title: "Apply the age modifier.",
    fourStep3Desc: "Skiers under 10 years old or 50 and older move one row higher on the chart (-1 code reduction) to account for bone and joint vulnerability. Skiers weighing 13 kg or less receive no age modifier.",
    fourStep4Title: "Cross-reference with Boot Sole Length (BSL).",
    fourStep4Desc: "Your final adjusted Skier Code selects the row in the ISO 11088 matrix; your Boot Sole Length (BSL in mm) selects the column. The intersecting cell is your baseline DIN estimate.",
    bslTitle: "What Is Boot Sole Length (BSL)?",
    bslP1: "Boot Sole Length (BSL) is the total length of the ski boot's sole in millimeters, measured from heel lug to toe lug. It is permanently stamped or embossed on the heel lug or arch of every alpine ski boot shell. BSL is entirely different from Mondo sizing (your foot length in centimeters) — a size 27.5 Mondo boot from different manufacturers can have BSL values ranging from 298 mm to 320 mm.",
    bslP2: "BSL directly affects DIN because longer boots apply more leverage to the binding. A binding that correctly releases a 300 mm BSL boot may pre-release a 330 mm boot under the same force, or fail to release a 290 mm boot in a crash. Always use the exact stamped BSL value — never estimate from shoe size.",
    bslLinkText: "BSL & Mondo Sizing Guide →",
    skierTypeTitle: "Choosing Your Skier Type",
    skierTypeP1: "Selecting the correct Skier Type is critical — it is the most common error when people set their own DIN incorrectly. The ISO 11088 standard defines four categories:",
    skierTypeMinusI: "Extremely cautious beginner children who ski only gentle, groomed terrain at very slow speeds.",
    skierTypeI: "Cautious skiers who ski at moderate speeds on easier groomed runs. Prefer easy release above all else.",
    skierTypeII: "Average skiers who ski varied terrain at moderate-to-high speeds. The default for most adults.",
    skierTypeIII: "Aggressive, experienced skiers skiing difficult terrain at high speeds. Retention is prioritized over release.",
    skierTypeP2: "Most recreational adult skiers are Type I or Type II. Self-classifying as Type III when you are not leads to dangerous over-retention settings.",
    safetyTitle: "Is a DIN Calculator Safe to Use Without a Technician?",
    safetyP1: "DIN Calculator Pro provides an informational baseline reference derived from the published tables in ISO 11088:2023. This is a reference starting point, not a substitute for hands-on workshop service. The physical act of adjusting your binding, verifying forward pressure, and inspecting release tension must always be performed by a certified ski technician using calibrated torque test equipment.",
    safetyP2: "Binding release is affected by physical variables beyond lookup tables: boot wear at the toe and heel lugs, friction strip condition, forward pressure spring preload, binding mechanical tolerances, and pivot alignment. A mechanical torque inspection device measures actual release torque and allows adjustments that no digital calculator can provide.",
    safetyWorkflowTitle: "The recommended workflow:",
    safetyWorkflowText: "Use DIN Calculator Pro to calculate your reference DIN indicator, print or save your reference card, and take your equipment to a certified ski shop. A certified ski technician will set the indicator, verify forward pressure, and test your binding release within standard tolerances using calibrated workshop equipment.",
    subLinksMatrixTitle: "ISO 11088 Matrix",
    subLinksMatrixDesc: "Full interactive DIN table",
    subLinksBslTitle: "BSL Guide",
    subLinksBslDesc: "Find your boot sole length",
    subLinksSkierTypesTitle: "Skier Types",
    subLinksSkierTypesDesc: "Type I, II, III guide"
  }
};

const c = (homeContent as any)[lang] || homeContent.en;
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>

  <!-- HERO — Keyword-focused H1 & Value Proposition -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] dark:opacity-[0.04]" style="background-image: linear-gradient(var(--theme-hairline) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, var(--theme-hairline) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 48px 48px;"></div>
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[500px] h-[200px] rounded-full opacity-10 dark:opacity-[0.05] blur-3xl" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #FF6B00 0%, transparent 70%);"></div>

    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-4 pb-3 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight leading-tight mb-2 sm:mb-3">
        {lang === 'de' ? 'Z-Wert Rechner Skibindung' : lang === 'fr' ? 'Calculateur DIN Fixations de Ski' : lang === 'it' ? 'Calcolatore DIN Attacchi Sci' : 'Ski DIN Calculator'}
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-base text-mute max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-3 sm:mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        {lang === 'de' 
          ? 'Kostenloser Skibindungs-Rechner nach ISO 11088:2023. Ermitteln Sie Ihren Richtwert transparent in wenigen Sekunden.' 
          : lang === 'fr' 
          ? 'Calculateur de réglage DIN pour fixations de ski selon ISO 11088:2023. Gratuit, instantané et transparent.' 
          : lang === 'it' 
          ? 'Calcolo taratura attacchi da sci secondo la norma ISO 11088:2023. Gratuito, trasparente e immediato.' 
          : 'Free ski binding release calculator based on ISO 11088:2023 (Edition 7). Calculate your recommended DIN setting in seconds.'}
      </p>

      <div class="hidden sm:flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-5">
        <a href="#calculator" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-primary text-white font-semibold text-sm transition-all hover:opacity-90 hover:scale-[1.02] shadow-lg" style="box-shadow: 0 4px 24px -4px color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 50%, transparent);">
          {t('cta.calcMyDin')}
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href={getRouteFromUrl(new URL('/din-chart/', siteUrl), lang)} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-hairline bg-parchment text-ink font-medium text-sm transition-all hover:border-primary/50 hover:bg-canvas">
          {t('cta.matrixTable')}
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-[11px] sm:text-xs text-mute">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><svg class="w-3 h-3 text-emerald-500" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>Based on ISO 11088:2023</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><svg class="w-3 h-3 text-emerald-500" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>Cookieless & Private</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><svg class="w-3 h-3 text-emerald-500" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>Free & Open-Source</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       CALCULATOR SECTION
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="calculator" class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-1 sm:pt-4 pb-16">
    <!-- Divider label -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3 sm:mb-8">
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-hairline"></div>
      <span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-semibold text-mute uppercase tracking-widest px-3">Calculator</span>
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-hairline"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="min-h-[580px] w-full">
      <CalculatorApp client:load lang={lang} />
    </div>

    <!-- Trust Strip -->
    <div class="mt-6 p-4 rounded-xl bg-parchment border border-hairline flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-3 text-xs text-mute">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
        <span>Based on <strong>ISO 11088:2023</strong> (Edition 7) · Engine v2.0.0 · Independent project</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <a href="/methodology/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">Methodology & Limitations →</a>
        <a href="/changelog/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">Changelog →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ANSWER-FIRST BLOCK — Crawlable answers & worked example (ISO 11088:2023) -->
    <div class="mt-10 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-canvas border border-hairline shadow-sm space-y-6">
      <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">
          <span>{c.quickAnswerBadge}</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink">
          {c.quickAnswerH2}
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-mute leading-relaxed mt-2">
          {c.quickAnswerP}
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Worked Example & Quick Table Grid -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start">
        <!-- Worked Example Breakdown -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{c.exampleTitle}</h3>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-mute">ISO 11088:2023</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-parchment border border-hairline space-y-3 text-xs">
            <div class="flex justify-between py-1 border-b border-hairline/60">
              <span class="text-mute">{c.profile}</span>
              <span class="font-mono font-medium text-ink">{c.profileVal}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between py-1 border-b border-hairline/60">
              <span class="text-mute">{c.step1}</span>
              <span class="font-mono font-semibold text-ink">Code K</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between py-1 border-b border-hairline/60">
              <span class="text-mute">{c.step2}</span>
              <span class="font-mono font-semibold text-ink">Code K</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between py-1 border-b border-hairline/60">
              <span class="text-mute">{c.step3}</span>
              <span class="font-mono font-semibold text-ink">{c.step3Val}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between py-1 border-b border-hairline/60">
              <span class="text-mute">{c.step4}</span>
              <span class="font-mono font-semibold text-accent">{c.step4Val}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between py-1 border-b border-hairline/60">
              <span class="text-mute">{c.step5}</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-ink">{c.step5Val}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center pt-1 text-sm font-bold text-ink">
              <span>{c.step6}</span>
              <span class="text-primary font-mono text-base px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-parchment border border-hairline font-bold">DIN {workedExample.din}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-mute italic">
            {c.note}
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Quick Reference by Weight Table -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{c.tableTitle}</h3>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-mute">BSL 291–310 mm</span>
          </div>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-parchment">
            <table class="w-full text-xs text-left">
              <thead class="bg-input/70 border-b border-hairline text-mute font-mono">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2">{c.tableWeight}</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-center">{c.tableType1}</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-center font-semibold text-ink">{c.tableType2}</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-center">{c.tableType3}</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline font-mono">
                {quickTable.map((row) => (
                  <tr class="hover:bg-canvas/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="px-3 py-2 text-ink font-medium">{row.weight}</td>
                    <td class="px-3 py-2 text-center text-mute">{row.type1}</td>
                    <td class="px-3 py-2 text-center font-bold text-primary">{row.type2}</td>
                    <td class="px-3 py-2 text-center text-ink">{row.type3}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[11px] text-mute">
            <span>{c.exploreMore}</span>
            <a href="/din-chart/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">{c.fullMatrixLink}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       FEATURE PILLARS — 3-up grid
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-20 pt-4">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-12">
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-hairline"></div>
      <h2 class="text-[11px] font-mono font-semibold text-mute uppercase tracking-widest px-3">System Architecture & Standards</h2>
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-hairline"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      {c.pillars.map((pillar: any, idx: number) => (
        <div class="group p-7 rounded-2xl bg-parchment border border-hairline hover:border-primary/30 transition-all hover:shadow-md space-y-4">
          <div class={`w-10 h-10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center ${idx === 0 ? 'text-primary' : idx === 1 ? 'text-emerald-500 bg-emerald-500/10' : 'text-cyan-500 bg-cyan-500/10'}`} style={idx === 0 ? "background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 12%, transparent);" : ""}>
            {idx === 0 && <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/></svg>}
            {idx === 1 && <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 15v2m-6 4h12a2 2 0 002-2v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2zm10-10V7a4 4 0 00-8 0v4h8z"/></svg>}
            {idx === 2 && <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 17v-2m3 2v-4m3 4v-6m2 10H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"/></svg>}
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2">{pillar.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-mute leading-relaxed">{pillar.desc}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       HOW IT WORKS — 4-step methodology
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-14">
      <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold text-mute mb-3 block font-mono">Methodology</span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">{c.methodologyH2}</h2>
      <p class="text-mute mt-4 text-sm sm:text-base">{c.methodologyDesc}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      {c.methodologySteps.map((item: any, idx: number) => {
        const icons = [
          `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 3v18m0-18l8 6M12 3L4 9"/>`,
          `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 7h8m0 0v8m0-8l-8 8-4-4-6 6"/>`,
          `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/>`,
          `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v2a2 2 0 01-2 2H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6zM14 6a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v2a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2V6zM4 16a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v2a2 2 0 01-2 2H6a2 2 0 01-2-2v-2zM14 16a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v2a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2v-2z"/>`
        ];
        return (
          <div class="bg-parchment border border-hairline p-6 rounded-2xl text-center flex flex-col items-center group hover:border-primary/40 transition-all hover:shadow-md">
            <span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold text-primary mb-3 tracking-widest">{item.step}</span>
            <div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-2xl bg-canvas border border-hairline flex items-center justify-center text-primary mb-4 group-hover:border-primary/40 group-hover:bg-primary/5 transition-all">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.8" set:html={icons[idx]}></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 text-[15px]">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-mute leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</p>
          </div>
        );
      })}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       SEO LONG-FORM CONTENT — ~1000 words
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="prose-section space-y-10">

      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold text-mute mb-3 block font-mono">{lang === 'de' ? 'Vollständiger Leitfaden' : lang === 'fr' ? 'Guide Complet' : lang === 'it' ? 'Guida Completa' : 'Complete Guide'}</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">{c.guideH2}</h2>
        <p class="text-mute mt-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">{c.guideDesc}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">{c.dinDefTitle}</h3>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            {c.dinDefP1}
          </p>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            {c.dinDefP2}
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">{c.isoMattersTitle}</h3>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            {c.isoMattersP1}
          </p>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            {c.isoMattersP2}
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-parchment border border-hairline space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">{c.fourStepTitle}</h3>
        <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm text-mute">
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">1</span>
            <div><strong class="text-ink">{c.fourStep1Title}</strong> {c.fourStep1Desc}</div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">2</span>
            <div><strong class="text-ink">{c.fourStep2Title}</strong> {c.fourStep2Desc}</div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">3</span>
            <div><strong class="text-ink">{c.fourStep3Title}</strong> {c.fourStep3Desc}</div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">4</span>
            <div><strong class="text-ink">{c.fourStep4Title}</strong> {c.fourStep4Desc}</div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">{c.bslTitle}</h3>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            {c.bslP1}
          </p>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            {c.bslP2}
          </p>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <a href={getRouteFromUrl(new URL('/bsl-guide/', siteUrl), lang)} class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">{c.bslLinkText}</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">{c.skierTypeTitle}</h3>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
            {c.skierTypeP1}
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-mute">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-primary font-semibold shrink-0">Type −I</span> {c.skierTypeMinusI}</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-primary font-semibold shrink-0">Type I</span> {c.skierTypeI}</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-primary font-semibold shrink-0">Type II</span> {c.skierTypeII}</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-primary font-semibold shrink-0">Type III</span> {c.skierTypeIII}</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">{c.skierTypeP2}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">{c.safetyTitle}</h3>
        <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
          {c.safetyP1}
        </p>
        <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
          {c.safetyP2}
        </p>
        <p class="text-mute text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-ink">{c.safetyWorkflowTitle}</strong> {c.safetyWorkflowText}
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick links to sub-pages -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-4">
        <a href={getRouteFromUrl(new URL('/din-chart/', siteUrl), lang)} class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-parchment hover:border-primary/40 transition-all group">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 10h18M3 14h18M10 3v18M14 3v18"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">{c.subLinksMatrixTitle}</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-mute">{c.subLinksMatrixDesc}</div>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a href={getRouteFromUrl(new URL('/bsl-guide/', siteUrl), lang)} class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-parchment hover:border-primary/40 transition-all group">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 20l-5.447-2.724A1 1 0 013 16.382V5.618a1 1 0 011.447-.894L9 7m0 13l6-3m-6 3V7m6 10l4.553 2.276A1 1 0 0021 18.382V7.618a1 1 0 00-.553-.894L15 4m0 13V4m0 0L9 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">{c.subLinksBslTitle}</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-mute">{c.subLinksBslDesc}</div>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a href={getRouteFromUrl(new URL('/skier-types/', siteUrl), lang)} class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-parchment hover:border-primary/40 transition-all group">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">{c.subLinksSkierTypesTitle}</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-mute">{c.subLinksSkierTypesDesc}</div>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       FAQ SECTION
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-12">
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-hairline"></div>
      <span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-semibold text-mute uppercase tracking-widest px-3">FAQ</span>
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-hairline"></div>
    </div>
    <FaqSection lang={lang} />
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
